! mcp_bootstrap_p106.strap -- printed page 106:
! "******** SPECIAL MCP PSEUDO OPS ********", followed by the head
! of "******** INPUT COMMAND PARAMETERS ********".
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.113, header READ AND NOT ASSUMED:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP  CARD ID
! CB000106  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 106".  The TIME CLOCK
! 00054041 and the PUNID are the ones every page since printed p.97
! prints; the card-ID prefix is the "CB" that printed p.104 opened
! with (CB000001) and is read, not assumed -- see the line count.
!
! TWENTY-NINE LINES, AND THAT IS COUNTED, NOT ESTIMATED.  The
! rightmost column prints one card serial per line, CB000106 through
! CB000134 with no break, twenty-nine rows, and the printed line
! numbers run 1 to 29.  Below line 29 the page is blank (the bottom
! two thirds of the render carry only the form's rules).  Nothing
! fell off the top or the bottom.
!
! THE JOIN TO printed p.105 IS CLEAN: p.105's last serial is
! CB000105 (its line 56) and this page opens at CB000106, so this
! page is the next card of one punched deck with no break.
!
! >>> BUT CB000049 IS MISSING FROM THE PRINTED LISTING, AND THAT IS
! NOT MY PAGE'S DOING. <<<  Rendered and read at 600 dpi, printed
! p.104's last serial is CB000048 (its line 48) and printed p.105's
! first is CB000050 (its line 1).  One serial is skipped between
! those two pages.  Recorded here because the serial column is the
! tool every one of these decks uses to prove nothing fell off a
! page, and this is the first place it does NOT run consecutively.
! Whether card 49 was pulled, was a card the listing suppresses, or
! sits on a page edge is NOT examined here and nothing on p.106
! depends on it.
!
! >>> THE WHOLE PAGE IS DEFINITIONS AND NOT ONE CARD COMPILES A
! WORD. <<<  Eleven SYN cards define eleven symbols (lines 8-18);
! thirteen more SYN cards are COMMENTED OUT (lines 1-5 and 22-29);
! five cards are heading/spacer comment cards (lines 6, 7, 19, 20,
! 21).  11 + 13 + 5 = 29.  So this deck's entire check surface is
! ELEVEN SYMBOLS AND ZERO LISTING ROWS -- printed p.99's convention,
! which pp.101, 102 and 104 also follow: a SYN deposits no storage
! word, so it is checked in !SYM and must NOT be faked into a
! !CHECK.  There are no !CHECK lines below and that is correct.
!
! >>> THERE IS NO SLC ON THIS PAGE AND THE DECK WRITES NONE. <<<
! Nothing here emits storage, so the location counter arrives and
! leaves untouched, and no row on the page states it.  (printed
! p.104 line 6 is the last SLC seen, "SLC,$" printed 215020.71.)
! Every LOCATION printed here ends in "+" and is a SYN's RESOLVED
! VALUE relative to a zero base -- a pseudo-op code, not an address.
! THERE IS NO ADDRESS CHAIN TO CLOSE ACROSS THIS PAGE and none
! should be attempted.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! It continues printed pp.104-105's MCP PSEUDO-OPERATION CODE
! TABLE.  p.104 defines the service pseudo-ops a problem program
! may request ($RD at 1.0 through $CHEX at 12.0); p.105 carries
! $IODEF and the $SIO..$SCR group and then two reserved blocks;
! this page defines the ELEVEN MAJOR-PACKAGE PSEUDO-OPS, the codes
! by which MCP's own major packages (job control, the loggers, the
! debugger, the command programs) call each other through $MCP.
! Each code is a word.bit pair at .0 or .32, and the eleven run
! consecutively from 76.32 to 81.32 with no gap.
!
! >>> THE NAMES AND THE CODES ARE CONFIRMED BY A PRIMARY SOURCE,
! NAME FOR NAME AND NUMBER FOR NUMBER. <<<
! docs/C22-6728_7030_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide.pdf, FIGURE 14, "MAJOR
! PACKAGE PSEUDO-OPS", printed p.29 (PDF p.29 of that scan), prints
! a two-column table whose right half is:
!
!     SJC1    Job Control 1        76.32
!     SOUTPT  Output Command       77.00
!     SSPEOJ  Output EOJ           77.32
!     SDDT    Debugger             78.00
!     SJC4    IPL Entry to JC4     78.32
!     SSCR4   First Card Request   79.00
!     SKOM    Input Commands       79.32
!     SCOMD   System Commands      80.00
!     SLOG4   Logger 4             80.32
!     SLOG2   Logger 2             81.00
!     SLOG1   Logger 1             81.32
!
! -- eleven names in this page's order, with this page's codes, and
! with descriptions that are this page's own comment column almost
! word for word ("IPL Entry to JC4" / "-IPL ENTRY TO JC4", "Input
! Commands" / "-INPUT COMMANDS", "First Card Request" /
! "-$SCR+N.32,N=10.0 1ST CARD REQ.").
!
! ONE OF THE ELEVEN DESCRIPTIONS DOES NOT MATCH, AND IT IS NAMED
! RATHER THAN GLOSSED: SOUTPT is "Output Command" in Figure 14 and
! "-OUTPUT TAPE SWITCH" on this page.  The name and the code agree;
! only the gloss differs, and the two documents are not the same
! date.  Nothing here depends on either wording.
!
! That settles BY DOCUMENT
! every glyph on this page that shape alone cannot -- see the GLYPH
! section below, where four round glyphs were decided by
! measurement first and then found to agree with this table.
!
! >>> AND THE REVISION OF THAT MANUAL IS THE WRONG ONE TO USE. <<<
! docs/C22-6728-1_7030_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide.pdf is the LATER
! printing and its FIGURE 15 carries the SAME ELEVEN NAMES IN THE
! SAME ORDER WITH ALL ELEVEN CODES MOVED UP BY EXACTLY 3.0 WORDS
! (SJC1 79.32 ... SLOG1 84.32).  This March 1963 listing agrees
! with the UNREVISED C22-6728 and not with C22-6728-1.  Anyone
! checking these codes against a manual must check which printing
! they have; the -1 would make all eleven look wrong by 3.0.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PAGE LINE BY LINE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 1-5   FIVE COMMENTED-OUT SYN CARDS, printed with an EMPTY
!             NAME field and the statement "$SYN,74.0", "$SYN,74.32",
!             "$SYN,75.0", "$SYN,75.32", "$SYN,76.0".  They continue
!             printed p.105 line 55's heading "******** RESERVED FOR
!             INSTALLATION PSEUDO OPS ********": p.105 lines 44-53
!             are the identical form "$SYN,69.0" .. "$SYN,73.32"
!             under "RESERVED FOR FUTURE MCP USE".  So codes 69.0
!             through 76.0 are reserved placeholders and line 8
!             picks the table up again at 76.32 with no gap.
!             LINE 2 CARRIES A COMMENT and the others do not:
!             "-UNCONDITIONA $SCR RESLD - TEMPORARY" (the page
!             prints UNCONDITIONA, twelve letters, with no final L;
!             read twice at 600 dpi).  So the 74.32 slot is in
!             temporary use for an unconditional $SCR/$RESLD.
! Line 6      "******** SPECIAL MCP PSEUDO OPS ********"
! Line 7      spacer comment card
! Lines 8-18  THE ELEVEN COMPILED SYN CARDS, transcribed below.
! Lines 19,21 spacer comment cards
! Line 20     "******** INPUT COMMAND PARAMETERS********"  (the page
!             prints no blank between PARAMETERS and the asterisks)
! Lines 22-29 EIGHT COMMENTED-OUT SYN CARDS, the parameter values
!             passed with SKOM:
!               22  - S ONL   SYN,0      -ON-LINE
!               23  - S OFF   SYN,.32    -OFFLINE
!               24  - S EOF   SYN,1.0    -END OF FILES
!               25  - S EJSCNSYN,1.32    -EOJ SCAN
!               26  - S BYP   SYN,2.0    -BYPASS
!               27  - S REW   SYN,2.32   -REWIND
!               28  - S CR1   SYN,3.0    -JC1 CARD REQUEST
!               29  - S CAN   SYN,3.32   -PHASE ONE SCAN
!             NONE of these is faked into a !SYM: a commented card
!             defines nothing.  They are recorded because the same
!             parameter codes appear in C22-6728's SKOM calling
!             sequences ("(3.0) , SKOM", "(1.32) , SKOM", "(0.0) ,
!             SKOM"), which is a second reading of the numbers.
!
! >>> HOW THE COMMENTED CARDS WERE IDENTIFIED, AND THE DASH IS NOT
! THE TELL. <<<  Measured at 1200 dpi, the first printed character
! of lines 6, 7, 19, 20, 21 and 22-29 is a "-" sitting in the SAME
! character cell as the NAME field of lines 8-18 (x = 2351 vs 2358
! at 300 dpi, a quarter of the 29.7 px character pitch -- the same
! cell, not the cell to its left).  LINES 1-5 PRINT NO DASH AT ALL.
! So a dash neither marks every comment card nor is confined to a
! column of its own, exactly as printed p.103 found.  The two tells
! that do hold for all thirteen are printed p.104's:
!   (i)  LOCATION and BINARY OUTPUT are BOTH empty, and
!   (ii) the fields DO NOT LINE UP.  Line 25 prints
!        "S EJSCNSYN,1.32" with NO GAP before SYN -- a six-character
!        name run straight into the statement -- which no compiled
!        row on this page does; all eleven print NAME and STATEMENT
!        in their own columns.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE BINARY OUTPUT COLUMN ON A DEFINITIONS PAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! All eleven compiled rows print "+00000000" in the value field and
! the data description "NULL".  That is the column working
! correctly: a SYN with no mode has a NULL data description, and
! the eleven cards carry none.  It is NOT machine code and NOT a
! crop landing in the wrong place, and it is not checked here.
!
! THE PAGE CHECKS ITS OWN DIGITS.  Each SYN prints its offset in
! DECIMAL in the STATEMENT column and the same offset in OCTAL in
! the LOCATION column, and all eleven agree:
!   76.32/000114.40  77.0/000115.00  77.32/000115.40
!   78.0/000116.00   78.32/000116.40 79.0/000117.00
!   79.32/000117.40  80.0/000120.00  80.32/000120.40
!   81.0/000121.00   81.32/000121.40
! (76 = 0o114, 81 = 0o121, 32 = 0o40.)  That is a real check of the
! digits, though not of the card.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TWO OF THE ELEVEN ARE ALREADY IN THE CORPUS, AND THEY AGREE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p35.strap lines 110-111 carry
!   SJC4  SYN, 78.32    000116.40
!   SCOMD SYN, 80.0     000120.00
! back-derived from printed p.33's operands ", S JC4" and
! ", S COMD" (p.33 line 43, and lines 27 and 36).  This page
! DECLARES both at exactly those values.  So this is NOT the
! DFREE-style cross-deck collision printed p.104 reports: it is a
! corroboration, and it is also an independent check on the two
! spellings, since p.33/p.35 read them off a different page in a
! different punched deck.  The other nine names appear nowhere else
! in the corpus.
!
! TAIL SCOPE, RECORDED AND NOT "FIXED".  printed p.99 line 11's
! "SLC,(8)215000." put pp.99+ outside the TAIL,(2)G block that
! printed p.2 opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed with
! "UNTAIL,(2)", so a name here may legitimately repeat a pp.2-98
! name at a different value.  None of these eleven does: the only
! two that recur recur at the SAME value.  Note separately that
! tests/verify_mcp_bootstrap_p4.py carries X9A3A at 000114.40 and
! X9A5 at 000121.40 -- the same octal strings as lines 8 and 18 --
! but those are IPL STORAGE ADDRESSES and these are SYN VALUES in a
! zero-based pseudo-op code space.  Different kinds of number that
! happen to print alike; not a collision of any sort.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS: FOUR ROUND CHARACTERS, MEASURED BEFORE THEY WERE LOOKED UP
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> ON THIS PAGE AN O IN THE NAME COLUMN IS ROUTINELY PRINTED
! OPEN, SO SHAPE ALONE IS A COIN FLIP. <<<  Proof, not impression:
! tesseract run on the name column at 1200 dpi returns
!   SJCl SCUTPT SSPECJ SLCT SJC4 SSCR4 SKCM SCCMD SLCG4 SLCG2 SLCG1
! -- it reads EVERY round glyph as C, including the five that are
! certainly O (SOUTPT's, SCOMD's, and the three LOGGER O's).  Nine
! round glyphs in that column have known values (four C from JC1,
! JC4, SCR and COMD; five O from OUTPT, COMD and the three LOGs)
! and a second reader called all nine C.
!
! WHAT WAS DONE INSTEAD.  The eleven names were segmented into
! glyph bitmaps, size-normalised, and each round glyph scored by
! intersection-over-union against the KNOWN O's and KNOWN C's OF
! THE SAME COLUMN OF THE SAME PAGE.  Leave-one-out over the nine
! knowns classifies 9 of 9 correctly (C margins .06-.12, O margins
! .07-.17).  Run on the four unknown glyphs it gives
!   line 10, 5th glyph   O (.729 vs C .676)   -> SSPEOJ
!   line 11, 2nd glyph   D (.551, C .557, O .533 -- A TIE)
!   line 11, 3rd glyph   D (.671 vs O .603, C .588)
!   line 14, 3rd glyph   O (.799 vs C .664)   -> SKOM
! (the D template is SCOMD's own D, the only known D in the
! column).  The line 11 pair's best match is EACH OTHER (.593),
! which is the argument for reading them as the same letter.
! ONLY THEN was C22-6728 Figure 14 opened, and it gives SSPEOJ,
! SDDT, SKOM.  Four for four, including the glyph the measurement
! called a tie.
!
! The two round glyphs that are NOT ambiguous are recorded too:
!   * SOUTPT's O (line 9) prints CLOSED, the only closed round
!     glyph in the column, and the comment "-OUTPUT TAPE SWITCH"
!     names the word.
!   * SJC1's and SJC4's C (lines 8, 12) are C by their comments,
!     "-JOB CONTROL PHASE ONE" and "-IPL ENTRY TO JC4".
!
! THE STATEMENT COLUMN DROPS INK ON ROUND GLYPHS TOO, AND IT COSTS
! NOTHING HERE.  Lines 9, 11, 15 and 17 print their bit offset as
! "SYN,77.C", "SYN,78.C", "SYN,80.C" and "SYN,81.C" where the
! offset is 0.  All four are settled by the LOCATION column, which
! prints 000115.00, 000116.00, 000120.00 and 000121.00 -- an octal
! field cannot hold a C.  (printed p.104's deck records three rows
! of the same kind.)  No statement on this page has a legal reading
! with a C in that position.
!
! $ IS NOT S ON THIS PAGE AND THE PAGE PROVES IT ITSELF.  Lines 1-5
! print "$SYN" and line 13's comment prints "-$SCR+N.32", both with
! the vertical bar clearly struck, while all eleven names begin
! with a bare S.  The first glyph of the names is therefore an S
! and not a worn $ -- which matters, because printed pp.104-105
! name their pseudo-ops with a "D " prefix ("D RD", "D SCR") and
! these eleven with an "S", and C22-6728 Figure 14 confirms the S.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS AND OMISSIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page
!     since printed p.2.  This page punches its names WITHOUT
!     blanks -- the glyph segmentation measures a uniform 29.7 px
!     pitch across all eleven, with no missing cell -- while
!     printed p.33's operands punch ", S JC4" and ", S COMD" WITH
!     one.  Both reduce to the same symbol, which is why p.35's
!     deck and this one agree.
! (2) THE THIRTEEN COMMENTED-OUT SYN CARDS AND THE FIVE HEADING AND
!     SPACER CARDS ARE NOT TRANSCRIBED.  Their text is recorded
!     above, verbatim.
! (3) Nothing else is substituted.  No printed spelling on this
!     page was rejected by strap_asm.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CARDS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The offsets are written EXACTLY AS THE STATEMENT COLUMN PRINTS
! THEM -- bare decimal literals, so "76.32" is word 76 decimal, bit
! 32 decimal, and resolves to 0o114.40, which is what the LOCATION
! column prints.  (The octal-inside-(8) rule does not apply: there
! is no (8) literal on this page.)

SJC1    SYN, 76.32                  ! line  8  S JC1    -JOB CONTROL PHASE ONE
SOUTPT  SYN, 77.0                   ! line  9  S OUTPT  -OUTPUT TAPE SWITCH
SSPEOJ  SYN, 77.32                  ! line 10  S SPEOJ  -OUTPUT EOJ
SDDT    SYN, 78.0                   ! line 11  S DDT    -DEBUGGER
SJC4    SYN, 78.32                  ! line 12  S JC4    -IPL ENTRY TO JC4
SSCR4   SYN, 79.0                   ! line 13  S SCR4   -$SCR+N.32,N=10.0 1ST CARD REQ.
SKOM    SYN, 79.32                  ! line 14  S KOM    -INPUT COMMANDS
SCOMD   SYN, 80.0                   ! line 15  S COMD   -SYSTEM COMMANDS
SLOG4   SYN, 80.32                  ! line 16  S LOG4   -LOGGER 4
SLOG2   SYN, 81.0                   ! line 17  S LOG2   -LOGGER 2
SLOG1   SYN, 81.32                  ! line 18  S LOG1   -LOGGER 1

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, DECLARED FOR listing_oracle
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Eleven symbols.  ZERO listing rows: every row on this page is a
! SYN and a SYN deposits no storage word, so there is nothing for
! the BINARY OUTPUT half of the oracle to check and nothing is
! invented for it.

!SYM   SJC1     000114.40
!SYM   SOUTPT   000115.00
!SYM   SSPEOJ   000115.40
!SYM   SDDT     000116.00
!SYM   SJC4     000116.40
!SYM   SSCR4    000117.00
!SYM   SKOM     000117.40
!SYM   SCOMD    000120.00
!SYM   SLOG4    000120.40
!SYM   SLOG2    000121.00
!SYM   SLOG1    000121.40
